========================================================================
VERDICT
========================================================================

**FAIL as isolated check of dirty sh/fs/f20.** Three `oodac check` rails
rc=1 on `undefined variable 'oo_fs_rmdir'`.

**PASS as compiler proof.** `./oodac/oodac check oodac/main.oo` rc=0,
wall **27.41s**, peak RSS **~12.50 GiB**. Not cheap. Not 1.7 s / 41 MB.

This does **not** prove:

- `std/sh.oo` is a sealed shell facade (check did not finish; does not inject)
- `std/os/fs.oo` landlock / writedir / rmdir / remove_tree (check does not open files)
- `harness_f20_inventory_smoke.oo` counts 39 std files (this is typecheck)
- a rebuilt ELF would accept `oo_fs_rmdir` (not rebuilt)
- the product rail is green

Do not say the product rail is green. Do not treat rc=0 on main as a
ci_product PASS. Do not treat rc=1 on the three as a source-tree lie;
it is ELF/source skew under a no-rebuild order.

